en-US.description:
Breaking the silence, a massive silhouette appeared off the coast of Gibraltar. It is the USS Alaska (SSBN-732), an Ohio-class nuclear-powered ballistic missile submarine known as the "Silent Warrior" and the U.S. Navy's premier strategic asset. It is highly unusual for the location of a nuclear submarine, whose very essence lies in stealth, to be exposed so publicly.

This deployment took place immediately after President Donald Trump rejected Iran's ceasefire proposal as "completely unacceptable garbage." Iran had demanded the lifting of sanctions, recognition of sovereignty over the Strait of Hormuz, and the withdrawal of U.S. troops through Pakistani mediation, but the Trump administration's response was firm. Instead of diplomatic negotiations, the United States chose to demonstrate its most powerful nuclear deterrent directly before the eyes...

